# Overlay build: the official 4.51 image with one patched binary.
#
# 4.51 carries everything the 4.48 overlay (@baba0ee) backported: the
# remote-only rename fix (#11709), #11514, #11515, #11569, #11574, #11581,
# #11584 and the same-second rewrite fix (#11715). Checked by ancestry on the
# merge commits, not by release notes.
#
# What is left is one daemon fix, ours and not upstream yet: isSuperseded also
# skips an event when the filer holds chunks the event did not. A mount
# flushes metadata while chunk uploads are still running, so a big file copied
# in through FUSE logs a create whose chunk list has holes. The stream reader
# stops at the first hole, every retry sends a short multipart body, and the
# old subset check kept the event live, so the daemon looped on it forever and
# nothing after it in the log reached the remote (2026-10-13, media sync). The
# later event with the finished chunk list uploads the file.
#
# Sent upstream as seaweedfs#12176. It leaves one case open: a writer that
# dies keeps its hole, nothing ever writes past it, and the event still
# loops. chrislusf's follow-up seaweedfs#12178 (not merged yet) closes it,
# and its three commits are cherry-picked here: the upload streams the
# entry's declared size through ChunkReadAt, which zero-fills every range no
# chunk covers, the same bytes a read of the entry returns. A sparse file
# uploads its zeros instead of a truncated object, and a mid-write snapshot
# uploads a zero-filled view that the finishing write's event replaces. The
# guards that keep a remote-only entry from being uploaded at all are
# unchanged.
#
# All of it is in `weed filer.remote.sync` only, so the Seaweed CR can run the
# stock 4.51 tag; only the two remote-sync Deployments need this image. Drop
# it when a release contains #12176 and #12178.
#
# The stock image reports `version 30GB 4.51 ffa87c25f`: the release build ran
# one CI-only commit past the tag (#12070, nothing under weed/). This build
# stamps its own commit instead.
#
# Deliberately NOT a fork of docker/Dockerfile.go_build. That file clones from
# github.com/seaweedfs/seaweedfs at build time, so it would silently ignore
# this branch's patches and produce a stock binary. It also builds the Rust
# volume server and maintenance worker, or pulls them from CI artifacts;
# reproducing that here would mean reproducing the whole release pipeline for
# no gain. Taking the published image as the base keeps every other byte
# (entrypoint, Rust binaries, labels) exactly as shipped, so the delta really
# is the commits on this branch.
ARG BASE=chrislusf/seaweedfs:4.51@sha256:f7a49e3f3972ebed5be2ed4befa4a0c68eb7bdddba6e692d42729ceb545134b8

FROM golang:1.26-alpine AS builder
RUN apk add --no-cache git
WORKDIR /src
COPY . .
ARG TARGETOS TARGETARCH
# Same flags as the upstream image build: CGO-free, statically linked, and the
# commit stamped into the version string so `weed version` identifies this
# build rather than claiming to be stock 4.51.
RUN cd weed \
  && export LDFLAGS="-X github.com/seaweedfs/seaweedfs/weed/util/version.COMMIT=$(git rev-parse --short HEAD)" \
  && export GOOS=${TARGETOS:-linux} GOARCH=${TARGETARCH:-amd64} \
  && CGO_ENABLED=0 go build -ldflags "-extldflags -static ${LDFLAGS}" -o /out/weed .

FROM ${BASE}
COPY --from=builder /out/weed /usr/bin/weed
